Market Trends
Shift to Silicon-Based Anodes: To achieve higher energy density, manufacturers are increasingly incorporating silicon into anode materials, though technical challenges remain.
Localization of Supply Chains: Geopolitical tensions and pandemic-related disruptions have accelerated the trend of localizing supply chains, with countries seeking to develop domestic capabilities.
Sustainability Focus: Increasing emphasis on circular economy principles is driving developments in recycling and use of recycled materials in new batteries.
Hybrid and Multi-Material Anodes: Combining different materials to optimize performance characteristics is becoming more common.
Advanced Manufacturing Techniques: Adoption of AI, IoT, and advanced automation in manufacturing processes to improve quality and reduce costs.
